{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6d96bb05-a4ed-4317-9e8a-ef818023debb",
    "name": "PropertyGpsApi - Single Plot GPS",
    "description": "BBMP Single Plot GPS backend.\n\nRun in order:\n1. Send OTP\n2. Verify OTP (paste the code; the token is saved automatically)\n3. Fetch applications\n\nIn Development no SMS is sent - the code is printed to the API console as \"DEV OTP for 9000000001 is 123456 (no SMS sent)\". You can also read it with:\n\n    SELECT TOP 1 OTP FROM OTP_Tran WHERE MobileNO = '9000000001' ORDER BY OTPID DESC;\n\nDo not retry with a wrong code: four failures deactivate the officer account.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "basePath",
      "value": "v1/api/gbagps/singlesite",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "appId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "applicationId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "epid",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/live",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "live"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Process is up. Touches no dependencies."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Round-trips both databases with SELECT 1. Check this first if anything else fails."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Send OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"mobile\": \"{{mobile}}\",\n    \"deviceId\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/auth/otp/send",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Generates a six-digit code and stores it via USP_I_OTP.\n\nIn Development the response also carries \"devOtp\" - the code itself - and the test script saves it to {{otp}}, so Verify OTP needs no editing. That field is only ever populated when the Development sender is in use; a deployed instance cannot return it.\n\nRate limited to 5 per 5 minutes per IP."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('OTP sent', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "if (body.success && body.data && body.data.devOtp) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('otp', body.data.devOtp);",
                  "    console.log('OTP captured: ' + body.data.devOtp + ' - just run Verify OTP next.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No devOtp in the response. That means a real SMS was sent, so read the code from the phone.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"mobile\": \"{{mobile}}\",\n    \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\",\n    \"deviceId\": \"postman\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "auth",
                "otp",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the code for a JWT.\n\nThe code comes from {{otp}}, which Send OTP filled in automatically. In production, replace it with the code from the SMS.\n\nOn success the token, corporationId, zoneId and wardId are saved to the environment.\n\nDo not retry with a wrong code: four failures deactivate the officer account."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('signed in', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "if (body.success && body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.environment.set('token', body.data.token);",
                  "    if (body.data.corporationId) pm.environment.set('corporationId', String(body.data.corporationId));",
                  "    if (body.data.zoneId) pm.environment.set('zoneId', String(body.data.zoneId));",
                  "    if (body.data.wardId) pm.environment.set('wardId', String(body.data.wardId));",
                  "    console.log('Token saved to the environment.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No token. ' + body.code + ': ' + body.message);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Masters",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Zones for a corporation",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/masters/zones",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "masters",
                "zones"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Zones in a corporation. Needed because sign-in returns ward names but not ward ids."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Wards in a zone",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/masters/wards",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "masters",
                "wards"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wards in a zone, with the ids the fetch request needs."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Property info",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Fetch applications",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"corporationId\": \"{{corporationId}}\",\n    \"zoneId\": \"{{zoneId}}\",\n    \"wardId\": \"{{wardId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/propertyinfo/fetch",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "propertyinfo",
                "fetch"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The ward worklist the app caches in SQLite.\n\nThe officer and role come from the token, never the body. A role-116 officer asking for another ward gets 403 OUTSIDE_JURISDICTION.\n\nAdd an \"epid\" field to filter to one application."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('fetched', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "const rows = (body.data || []);",
                  "const free = rows.find(function (r) { return r.assignedToUserId === null; });",
                  "const mine = rows.filter(function (r) { return r.isAssignedToMe; });",
                  "if (free) { pm.environment.set('appId', String(free.appId)); console.log('Next free appId: ' + free.appId); }",
                  "console.log('Total ' + rows.length + ', held by me ' + mine.length + ', held by others ' + rows.filter(function (r) { return r.isAssignedToOther; }).length);",
                  "const first = rows[0];",
                  "if (first) { pm.environment.set('applicationId', first.applicationId); pm.environment.set('epid', first.epid); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Allot to me",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"appId\": {{appId}}\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/propertyinfo/assign",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "propertyinfo",
                "assign"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Takes ownership of a record so it can be surveyed.\n\nThe officer comes from the token; the body carries only appId, which Fetch captured into {{appId}}.\n\nRejections are all 422 with recoverable=true:\n  ALREADY_ASSIGNED       - somebody else got there first\n  ASSIGNMENT_QUEUE_FULL  - you already hold two pending records\n  REASSIGN_LIMIT_REACHED - you have taken this same record too many times"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.success) { console.log('Allotted: ' + body.data.message); }",
                  "else { console.log('Rejected [' + body.code + ']: ' + body.message); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Release (unassign)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"appId\": {{appId}}\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/propertyinfo/unassign",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "propertyinfo",
                "unassign"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Hands a held record back to the pool. Backed by the same procedure via its IsActive flag.\n\nOnly works on a record you hold that is still Pending."
          },
          "event": [],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Report push status",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"items\": [\n        {\n            \"applicationId\": \"{{applicationId}}\",\n            \"epid\": \"{{epid}}\",\n            \"success\": true,\n            \"message\": \"Stored on device\"\n        }\n    ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/api/gbagps/singlesite/propertyinfo/push-status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "api",
                "gbagps",
                "singlesite",
                "propertyinfo",
                "push-status"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The device reporting which fetched applications it actually stored.\n\nAccepting one sets IsPushedToGps on BtoAMainApp, which is how the server stops offering it again - so this is what makes the ward download idempotent.\n\nSend up to 500 items. Each carries its own verdict, so one unknown application does not make the device re-send the batch:\n  \"GPS details updated successfully.\"  accepted, now marked pushed\n  \"This record is already pushed.\"     accepted, nothing to do\n  \"No matching application found.\"     unknown, or not at App_Status 10\n\nsuccess:false records the failure WITHOUT marking the record pushed, so the server will offer it again, and writes an application-wise row to the exception log.\n\nFetch captures the first record into {{applicationId}} and {{epid}}."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('recorded', function () { pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true); });",
                  "(body.data.results || []).forEach(function (r) {",
                  "    console.log((r.accepted ? 'OK   ' : 'SKIP ') + r.applicationId + ' - ' + r.message);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
